{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-382e8252fb87", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Van hits Berlin Pride crowd, one killed", "summary": "A van drove into a crowd at Berlin's Christopher Street Day on 25 July, killing one and injuring 16; police hunt a fleeing 21-year-old suspect.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/germany-launches-manhunt-after-berlin-pride-van-ramming/live-78117180", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["world", "security"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "A van drove into a crowd at Berlin's Christopher Street Day (the city's Pride march) late on Saturday 25 July, killing one person and injuring 16, three of them life-threateningly. The vehicle, a white transporter, struck marchers around 22:00 near Potsdamer Platz in the Tiergarten, and the parade was called off. Berlin police say they identified a fleeing suspect overnight — a 21-year-old man reported by German outlets as Abdul B. — and a citywide manhunt is under way; police describe him as having links to what they call the \"Islamist scene,\" a characterisation that comes from investigators and has not been confirmed by any court or established motive. Of the injured, eight are seriously and five lightly hurt.", "why": "It is the latest in a run of deadly vehicle-ramming attacks in Germany, and both the target — a Pride event — and the still-unproven motive will shape a charged domestic debate over security and extremism; treat the early \"Islamist\" framing as a police working theory, not a settled fact.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-van-hits-berlin-pride-crowd-one-killed", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Berlin", "Germany", "Christopher Street Day"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-van-hits-berlin-pride-crowd-one-killed"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-382e8252fb87", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "A van drove into a crowd at Berlin's Christopher Street Day (the city's Pride march) late on Saturday 25 July, killing one person and injuring 16, three of them life-threateningly. The vehicle, a white transporter, struck marchers around 22:00 near Potsdamer Platz in the Tiergarten, and the parade was called off. Berlin police say they identified a fleeing suspect overnight — a 21-year-old man reported by German outlets as Abdul B. — and a citywide manhunt is under way; police describe him as having links to what they call the \"Islamist scene,\" a characterisation that comes from investigators and has not been confirmed by any court or established motive. Of the injured, eight are seriously and five lightly hurt.", "why": "It is the latest in a run of deadly vehicle-ramming attacks in Germany, and both the target — a Pride event — and the still-unproven motive will shape a charged domestic debate over security and extremism; treat the early \"Islamist\" framing as a police working theory, not a settled fact.", "importance": 3, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-c233bbb5f7da", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "UN warns against wider US-Iran war", "summary": "The UN warned on 24 July of wider escalation and threats to Strait of Hormuz shipping as US strikes on Iran paused for a second day.", "url": "https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/07/1168016", "source_domain": "news.un.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["single-source", "ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The UN warned on Friday 24 July against a wider escalation in the US–Iran war and flagged the risk to global shipping in the Strait of Hormuz, as US strikes on Iran paused for a second day. The Strait is the narrow waterway carrying roughly a fifth of the world's oil; the warning came amid renewed Houthi attacks in the Red Sea. US Central Command, meanwhile, says its naval blockade of Iran \"remains in force\" — so the two-day lull in strikes is a pause, not a settlement, and earlier US framing of a \"final\" round of strikes has not held up.", "why": "Any closure of Hormuz or spread of the fighting to Red Sea shipping lanes would ripple straight into energy prices and supply chains far from the war zone.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-un-warns-against-wider-us-iran-war", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "United States", "Strait of Hormuz", "United Nations"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-un-warns-against-wider-us-iran-war"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-c233bbb5f7da", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "The UN warned on Friday 24 July against a wider escalation in the US–Iran war and flagged the risk to global shipping in the Strait of Hormuz, as US strikes on Iran paused for a second day. The Strait is the narrow waterway carrying roughly a fifth of the world's oil; the warning came amid renewed Houthi attacks in the Red Sea. US Central Command, meanwhile, says its naval blockade of Iran \"remains in force\" — so the two-day lull in strikes is a pause, not a settlement, and earlier US framing of a \"final\" round of strikes has not held up.", "why": "Any closure of Hormuz or spread of the fighting to Red Sea shipping lanes would ripple straight into energy prices and supply chains far from the war zone.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-0a9ec1ba66a5", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Wildfires shorten Tour de France finale", "summary": "Wildfires in southwest France and Spain forced mass evacuations and shortened the Tour de France's final Paris stage on 26 July.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/7/26/tour-de-france-final-stage-shortened-as-emergency-teams-tackle-wildfires", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Wildfires across southwestern France and Spain forced mass evacuations over the weekend and pushed organisers to shorten the final stage of the Tour de France on Sunday 26 July. The traditional closing ride was cut from 133 km to 89 km and rerouted onto the Champs-Élysées after security officers were pulled off the race to help fight blazes near Bordeaux; UN agencies put the number driven from their homes by Europe's fires this month above 250,000.", "why": "An exceptionally hot, dry European summer is now colliding with public life — evacuations, a diverted flagship sporting event — and the same drought is being felt in Switzerland.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-wildfires-shorten-tour-de-france-finale", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Spain", "Tour de France"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-wildfires-shorten-tour-de-france-finale"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-0a9ec1ba66a5", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Wildfires across southwestern France and Spain forced mass evacuations over the weekend and pushed organisers to shorten the final stage of the Tour de France on Sunday 26 July. The traditional closing ride was cut from 133 km to 89 km and rerouted onto the Champs-Élysées after security officers were pulled off the race to help fight blazes near Bordeaux; UN agencies put the number driven from their homes by Europe's fires this month above 250,000.", "why": "An exceptionally hot, dry European summer is now colliding with public life — evacuations, a diverted flagship sporting event — and the same drought is being felt in Switzerland.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-0170c01f80bb", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Brazil denies visas to US envoys", "summary": "Brazil refused entry visas to two planned US envoys, accusing Washington of trying to influence its coming presidential election.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-denies-entry-to-senior-trump-officials-ahead-of-elections/a-78117458", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Brazil refused entry visas to two planned US envoys, accusing Washington of trying to influence its coming presidential election. The move deepens a rift between Brasília and Washington that already includes US tariffs on Brazilian goods, and it lands as Flávio Bolsonaro — a senator and son of former president Jair Bolsonaro — secured his party's nod to run against President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva.", "why": "It is an unusually direct rebuff of the US by a major non-aligned democracy, and signals how sharply the Trump administration's tariff-and-pressure approach is straining relations across the Americas.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-brazil-denies-visas-to-us-envoys", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Brazil", "United States", "Flavio Bolsonaro", "Lula"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-brazil-denies-visas-to-us-envoys"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-0170c01f80bb", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Brazil refused entry visas to two planned US envoys, accusing Washington of trying to influence its coming presidential election. The move deepens a rift between Brasília and Washington that already includes US tariffs on Brazilian goods, and it lands as Flávio Bolsonaro — a senator and son of former president Jair Bolsonaro — secured his party's nod to run against President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva.", "why": "It is an unusually direct rebuff of the US by a major non-aligned democracy, and signals how sharply the Trump administration's tariff-and-pressure approach is straining relations across the Americas.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-e357991db30d", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Typhoon Noul makes landfall in China", "summary": "Typhoon Noul hit Guangdong province and Hong Kong on 26 July, forcing hundreds of thousands to evacuate.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/26/typhoon-noul-makes-landfall-in-china-with-hundreds-of-thousands-evacuated", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Typhoon Noul made landfall in southern China on Sunday 26 July, hitting Guangdong province and neighbouring Hong Kong with strong winds and heavy rain after hundreds of thousands were evacuated. Authorities across the Pearl River Delta ordered pre-emptive evacuations and suspended transport ahead of the storm.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-typhoon-noul-makes-landfall-in-china", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Typhoon Noul", "China", "Hong Kong", "Guangdong"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-typhoon-noul-makes-landfall-in-china"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
