{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-8ee6882ed9fa", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Breitling CEO seeks US watch-tariff waiver", "summary": "Breitling chief Georges Kern publicly urged Washington to exempt Swiss watches from the new 12.5% US tariff.", "url": "https://www.nzz.ch/wirtschaft/breitling-chef-george-kern-lobbyiert-in-den-usa-uhrenindustrie-hofft-auf-zollbefreiung-ld.10016871", "source_domain": "nzz.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Breitling chief executive Georges Kern publicly appealed to Washington on Saturday 25 July to exempt Swiss watches from US tariffs, arguing that America has no watch industry to protect. In an interview with the NZZ am Sonntag, Kern said tariffs are \"protectionism, but there are sectors the Americans have no need to protect because they simply don't have them,\" and that Swiss watches belong in that category. His plea follows the new 12.5% US duty on Swiss goods that took effect on Friday 24 July — imposed under a US \"forced labour\" rationale that Switzerland's business federation economiesuisse rejects as baseless, noting forced labour is already banned under Swiss constitutional and criminal law.", "why": "It is the first prominent Swiss-industry attempt to carve out a sector-specific escape from the tariff, and shows exporters betting on lobbying rather than waiting on Bern's trade talks.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-breitling-ceo-seeks-us-watch-tariff-waiver", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Breitling", "Georges Kern", "United States", "Switzerland"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-breitling-ceo-seeks-us-watch-tariff-waiver"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-8ee6882ed9fa", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Breitling chief executive Georges Kern publicly appealed to Washington on Saturday 25 July to exempt Swiss watches from US tariffs, arguing that America has no watch industry to protect. In an interview with the NZZ am Sonntag, Kern said tariffs are \"protectionism, but there are sectors the Americans have no need to protect because they simply don't have them,\" and that Swiss watches belong in that category. His plea follows the new 12.5% US duty on Swiss goods that took effect on Friday 24 July — imposed under a US \"forced labour\" rationale that Switzerland's business federation economiesuisse rejects as baseless, noting forced labour is already banned under Swiss constitutional and criminal law.", "why": "It is the first prominent Swiss-industry attempt to carve out a sector-specific escape from the tariff, and shows exporters betting on lobbying rather than waiting on Bern's trade talks.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-5af293e1ee81", "date": "2026-07-26", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss cantons ban 1 August fireworks", "summary": "Several cantons issued fireworks bans for the 1 August holiday as a weeks-long drought keeps open-fire restrictions in force.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/stiller-nationalfeiertag-kantone-erlassen-feuerwerksverbote-fuer-1-august-die-uebersicht", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Several Swiss cantons have issued explicit fireworks bans for the 1 August national holiday as a weeks-long drought keeps most of the country under open-fire restrictions. With near-total bans on open fires already in place across much of Switzerland — Zürich and Winterthur, for instance, prohibit even charcoal grilling in public — cantons have in recent days tightened the rules specifically for fireworks ahead of Saturday 1 August, meaning the traditional displays will be barred almost everywhere.", "why": "It is a concrete, everyday sign of the same European heat-and-drought spell driving the wildfires abroad, and it reshapes how the country's biggest civic holiday will be marked this year.", "thread_id": "2026-07-02-news-heatwave-absolute-fire-bans-imposed-in-valais-an", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-02", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Zurich", "Winterthur"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "updated": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-07-26-news-swiss-cantons-ban-1-august-fireworks"], "editions": ["2026-07-26-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-07-26T10:10:52Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-5af293e1ee81", "edition": "2026-07-26-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Several Swiss cantons have issued explicit fireworks bans for the 1 August national holiday as a weeks-long drought keeps most of the country under open-fire restrictions. With near-total bans on open fires already in place across much of Switzerland — Zürich and Winterthur, for instance, prohibit even charcoal grilling in public — cantons have in recent days tightened the rules specifically for fireworks ahead of Saturday 1 August, meaning the traditional displays will be barred almost everywhere.", "why": "It is a concrete, everyday sign of the same European heat-and-drought spell driving the wildfires abroad, and it reshapes how the country's biggest civic holiday will be marked this year.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
